-- title:
--   The two non-maximal primes through t are the formal branches
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\pi$ be an element generating that maximal ideal, and let $w \ge 1$ be a natural number. Let $O$ be a noetherian local ring and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,(\pi^{w})$, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^{w}$. Let $t \in O$ be an element whose image in the completion is carried by $\iota$ to `const (π ^ w) π`, the class of the constant power series $\pi$. Let $\mathfrak p_1 \ne \mathfrak p_2$ be prime ideals of $O$, both containing $t$ and both different from the maximal ideal of $O$. The conclusion is a disjunction: either, for every $f \in O$, $f \in \mathfrak p_1$ exactly when $\iota$ of the image of $f$ in the completion lies in the ideal generated by `const (π ^ w) π` and the coordinate element `U (π ^ w)`, while $f \in \mathfrak p_2$ exactly when that image lies in the ideal generated by `const (π ^ w) π` and the other coordinate element `V (π ^ w)`; or the same two descriptions hold with the roles of `U (π ^ w)` and `V (π ^ w)` exchanged. Thus $\mathfrak p_1$ and $\mathfrak p_2$ are, in one order or the other, the contractions along $O \to \widehat{O} \xrightarrow{\iota} W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi^{w})$ of the two formal branch ideals $(\pi, U)$ and $(\pi, V)$.
--
--   This is the branch dictionary at an ordinary double point: a local ring whose completion is a crossing model has exactly two primes other than the maximal ideal containing the parameter $t$, and they are cut out by the two formal branches. It is used by the lemmas that set up node coordinates and branch readings on a curve with a node, where $O$ is the local ring at the node and $\iota$ the chosen identification of its completion.
